1
00:04:37,142 --> 00:04:43,142
You'll learn to love her. Warts and all.

2
00:09:14,285 --> 00:09:20,285
Nanny McPhee is a fantasy, comedy, family film directed by Kirk Jones.

3
00:13:51,428 --> 00:13:57,428
Widower Cedric Brown hires Nanny McPhee to care for his seven
rambunctious children, who have chased away all previous nannies.

4
00:18:28,571 --> 00:18:34,571
Taunted by Simon and his siblings, Nanny McPhee uses
mystical powers to instill discipline.

5
00:23:05,714 --> 00:23:11,714
And when the children's great-aunt and benefactor, Lady Adelaide Stitch, threatens to
separate the kids, the family pulls together under the guidance of Nanny McPhee.

6
00:27:42,857 --> 00:27:48,857
Nanny McPhee, played by Emma Thompson.

7
00:32:20,000 --> 00:32:26,000
Mr. Brown, played by Colin Firth.

8
00:36:57,142 --> 00:37:03,142
Evangeline, played by Kelly Macdonald.

9
00:41:34,285 --> 00:41:40,285
Simon, played by Thomas Brodie-Sangster.

10
00:46:11,428 --> 00:46:17,428
Tora, played by Eliza Bennett.

11
00:50:48,571 --> 00:50:54,571
Lily, played by Jennifer Rae Daykin.

12
00:55:25,714 --> 00:55:31,714
Nanny McPhee is a 2005 comedy drama fantasy film directed by Kirk Jones,
based on the Nurse Matilda character by Christianna Brand.

13
01:00:02,857 --> 01:00:08,857
Set in Victorian England in the 1860s, it stars Emma Thompson (who wrote the screenplay) as Nanny McPhee, along with Colin Firth,
Kelly Macdonald, Derek Jacobi, Celia Imrie, Patrick Barlow, Imelda Staunton, Thomas Sangster and Angela Lansbury.

14
01:04:40,000 --> 01:04:46,000
It was co-produced by StudioCanal, Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer Pictures, Working Title Films, Three Strange Angels, and Nanny
McPhee Productions with music by Patrick Doyle, and produced by Lindsay Doran, Tim Bevan and Eric Fellner.

15
01:09:17,142 --> 01:09:23,142
It was released theatrically on 28 October 2005 in the UK by United International
Pictures and on 27 January 2006 in the US by Universal Pictures.

16
01:13:54,285 --> 01:14:00,285
Thompson also scripted the film, which is adapted from
Christianna Brand's Nurse Matilda books.

17
01:18:31,428 --> 01:18:37,428
The filming location was Penn House Estate in Buckinghamshire.

18
01:23:08,571 --> 01:23:14,571
A sequel, Nanny McPhee and the Big Bang, was released in 2010.

19
01:27:45,714 --> 01:27:51,714
The film explores themes of loss of loved one, nanny,
education, family relationships, widower.

20
01:32:22,857 --> 01:32:28,857
The tone is lighthearted.
